Z||000000||Avery Montembeault||02-28-2001||05:30 PM||||I was thinking of swapping out my stock am/fm recciever and putting in  a CD player. I have one here but it doesnt fit the hole quite right, so I was thiking of putting a compartment/pocket thingie under the stereo...know where I can get one?||||reg||1
Z||000001||MontanaFiero||02-28-2001||05:43 PM||||Use a standard install kit. Sears has them for $15. Your aftermarket stereo WILL stick out about one inch, that's just the way it is, but with the kit it looks OK.<P>Your other alternative is to bend the stock bracket that supports the stock stereo in the back out of the way, but that's a pain in the a$$ and not worth the work. But if you still do it this way, make sure you support the back of the deck witht the strap that came with the unit.<P>------------------<BR>&gt;&gt; '87 Coupe 4 cyl, auto &lt;&lt;<BR>&gt;&gt; '86 SE V6, 4 speed- <I>project</I> &lt;&lt;||||reg||1
Z||000002||overlord||02-28-2001||07:14 PM||||how the heck to do you get the back of the radio on the suppport bracket at the back of the radio anyways!?!?!.    3 stereos ive  put in and could never figure that out, so all thats holding my raido in is the front supports||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||02-28-2001||07:25 PM||||Don't get the kit that causes the radio to stick out. It looks like cr@p and makes it difficult to put a CD in with the shifter in Park (on an auto trans) or in first, third or 5th depending on the manual trans you have. It takes about 10 seconds to remove the rear bracket.<BR>A long flat chisel or screwdriver. Line up on the rivot and smack it with a hammer. It pops right out. If you buy a decent adapter you don't need the rear support. If you buy a direct fit 1.5DIN radio you also do not need the support. If you really want to add it just take the strap that comes with the new radio and bolt it to the hole where the rivot was, slide radio in and from the rear of the console on the passenger side you can bend it and attach it if you'd like. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||stimpy||02-28-2001||11:33 PM||||Speaking of direct fit 1.5 DIN head units, I FINALLY received my Pioneer DEH-P77DH from competitionsound.com Just $230 including shipping and that thing bloody ROCKS! I still have to get the alarm function stuff hooked up and get it properly mounted, but I could not be happier with the sound. Just thought I'd share.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Black88GT||02-28-2001||11:38 PM||||Stimpy, you almost have me sold on this Pioneer unit.  Now that its in, any pics?||||reg||6
